# Deny everything, then name the four things the build actually needs. An allowlist rather
# than a deny list on purpose: a later COPY of a path nobody added here fails loudly at build
# time instead of silently shipping whatever the repository happens to hold.
#
# data/ is why this matters rather than merely being tidy: data/snapshots/, data/ledger/,
# data/handoffs/ and data/entries/ are gitignored precisely because captures and the entry
# payloads inside them are personal, and `docker build` does not read .gitignore.
*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!constraints.txt
!src

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[codz]
